    "declarations": "Parent-owned candidate03/presence.json supplies14 walking pairs and1ultimate pair with explicit absent/hidden/folded values. Independent actual-source review confirms14 near walking chains,14 far walking chains,2ultimate appendages and2antennae. This authoring does not infer or rewrite presence.",
    "visualAcceptance": "Bounded first source authoring for qualification. All main tips appear within the canvas. Requested8% margin remains missed; all delivered alpha/fringe is retained. No IC3, static, film, support or performance acceptance claimed.",
    "landmarkMethod": "All63 joint points and31fixed socket locations are manually authored from actual candidate03/master.png. No guide coordinates or rejected-master landmarks were copied. Source alpha was inspected at the drafted points; transparency misses were corrected by viewing local source crops, not by a nearest-pixel scan, a numerical grid, solver trials or motion-gate tuning. Some very thin distal tip points lie on retained low-alpha paint; no opacity cutoff is substituted for source alpha. Socket centers are visible lateral attachment estimates, not claims to see hidden internal joint centers.",
    "ownershipMethod": "Thirty-two owners:28 whole walking limbs,2ultimate appendages,one head andone rigid trunk/body remainder. Whole-limb polygons are explicit bounded envelopes constructed around the manually observed socket/knee/foot paths and visually chosen shaft widths; they are initial contour approximations, not measured segmentation. Near limbs precede far limbs, then ultimate appendages, head andbody remainder. Head includes its separate visible antennae and mouth paint. No extra texture owners or merged walking legs.",
    "regionalMethod": "Twenty-eight explicit proximal source extents seed their Knee while the uncovered lower spans retain the existing Foot split defaults. Three head extents seed mandible andeach antenna. All31regions have pin:false; this prototype does not request rigid locking of an entire multijoint texture. Source-pixel presence and eligible field-support membership are distinct; compiler refusals for shared/inherited pins or empty support selection must be retained rather than snapping regions.",
    "representationTradeoff": "Rigid trunk approximation with source-fixed head,28walking hip and2ultimate sockets. There are no seg0–seg7 channels and no independent trunk-wave claim. Each walking leg retains its own two movable spans; each ultimate appendage is a single controller retaining its bent silhouette without an independent knee. Body/leg/terminal part assignments do not imply hidden pixels were painted.",
    "framing": "groundLineY0.72 is a framing reference, not an inferred common terrain plane between near/far projected rows. The source is an elevated lateral view with far legs exposed above the trunk in projection.",
    "maskRepair": "Candidate04 same-paint ownership repair after intake01 refused contact/fixed-owner conflict. All28 walking envelopes now extend through the visible empty inter-limb gaps around the actual curved shafts anddistal extremities; local body-side collar cuts remain narrow at unchanged observed sockets. This uses explicit source-space polygon authoring, not nearest-joint pixel classification or a blanket body bounding-box transfer. Both ultimate outlines also follow their visible curved edges and adjoining fringe. No master alpha is discarded andall63landmarks,31sockets,31regional declarations,materials andpart ordering remain unchanged. First changed raster/field intake must judge the hypothesis; no fit or gate pass is claimed."
